 "verdict": "\u2b50 REORDERING. Spearman on arm levels 0.6631 (CI [0.6358, 0.7722]), R^2 of the margin regression 0.9063 (CI [0.8897, 0.9176]), slope 0.7142 (CI [0.6907, 0.7353]), against thresholds rho>=0.9 and R^2>=0.8. World A killed: True; world B killed: False. The synthetic compression world built from the 2B data returns rho 0.9379 and R^2 0.9929, so the design CAN recognise compression when it is present. Largest negative residuals: {'oracle_k4': -0.05818, 'oracle_k4_fit1': -0.05225, 'greedy_k4_fit1': -0.04621, 'promptecho_sham': -0.0298, 'promptecho': -0.02765}. \u2b50 AND THE PRACTICAL QUESTION IS NARROWER THAN THE GLOBAL ONE: of R1105's 9 sign-flipped arms, 5 are already predicted to flip by the COMPRESSION LINE ALONE, so their loss is a scale effect and renormalising the comparator would recover them; 4 are not. So the two mechanisms split the casualties and neither repair is sufficient alone.",
